maluos-installer (0.3.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Phase 11, the Apple T2 round. The facts know the Mac (model, the T2 chip,
    the bridge device) and every disk's partition table, free regions and
    sector size. storage.target free keeps the disk's partitions and installs
    into the largest free region, sharing the disk's EFI partition (UEFI only;
    sfdisk --append with explicit starts in the disk's sectors; a resume
    deletes the partitions it appended). On a T2 Mac the apple-t2 component is
    added when the medium carries it, the kernel gets intel_iommu=on iommu=pt
    pm_async=off, the initrd is rebuilt with apple-bce, and the Mac's Wi-Fi
    and Bluetooth firmware is imported (the apple sub-step). The on-media
    repository gains the extra pool of Ubuntu packages. The screens offer the
    free space on a disk that has some beside an EFI partition and pre-select
    the component on a Mac. efibootmgr uses the shared ESP's number and a
    Mac's refusal is a warning (EFI/BOOT boots the disk). Telemetry carries
    the Mac's model and the target.

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 22:30:00 +0000

maluos-installer (0.2.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Phase 11 slice 3: the screens. A medium booted without a plan shows the
    installer's urwid screens on the console (and `sudo maluos-install` on a
    serial line or over SSH): language and time zone, keyboard, network,
    storage with the guided layouts, LUKS and a typed confirmation of the
    disk, identity with the password's strength and SSH keys by paste or
    github:NAME, components from the medium's catalogue, first boot with the
    tenant, the administrator and an enrolment, "Help improve MaluOS" with
    the report shown, the summary with Save the plan, progress with the
    engine's events, done. Every screen writes to one plan (the contract of
    docs/install-plan.md), validated on every Continue; Install runs the
    engine in a thread. --screens [--plan FILE] prefills from a plan;
    --screens --no-hardware --save-plan OUT runs the screens without a
    machine (tests/install-screens-test.py drives them in a pty). The engine
    gained an event sink. Depends on python3-urwid, openssl, kbd.
  * The identity step generates the SSH host keys in the target when the
    plan enables the SSH server: the images ship none, and a desktop with
    cloud-init off had no sshd without them.

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 17:10:00 +0000

maluos-installer (0.1.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Phase 11 slice 2: the engine and the unattended install. maluos-install
    --plan executes an install plan (docs/install-plan.md): every step checked
    before the disk is touched (--check prints the plan as understood;
    --dry-run prints every command); storage (GPT, BIOS boot, ESP, /boot when
    separate, direct or LVM, ext4 or xfs, LUKS2 with argon2id), unpack (sha256
    against the medium's SHA256SUMS, unsquashfs -xattrs), configure (swap
    file, fstab and crypttab by UUID, hostname, locale, netplan, the user and
    SSH policy, the on-media repository, components from the catalogue,
    firstboot.yaml with enroll, cloud-init kept or disabled, grub defaults,
    the initrd for an encrypted root, machine-id), bootloader (the target's
    grub in the chroot for BIOS and UEFI with the signed shim; the NVRAM
    entry MaluOS first), finish (the log, the redacted plan and the journal
    into the target; one telemetry report when telemetry.send is true; the
    plan's action). Events on the log and, with --json, on stdout; a journal
    under /run/maluos-install makes --resume continue at the first sub-step
    not done. The console unit runs maluos.plan= or /maluos/plan/default.yaml.
    maluos-live-ssh.service (maluos.ssh=) for a remote install. --apt-check
    for tests/iso-apt-check.sh. --telemetry-preview.

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 13:10:00 +0000

maluos-installer (0.0.1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Phase 11 slice 1: the live medium's stub. maluos-install prints the
    banner and the medium's facts (--check-media: the medium, the live and
    target images with the target's SHA256 verified, the kernel, casper and
    the plymouth theme in the initrd, the firmware and Secure Boot state,
    the network) and leaves a root shell on tty1; with maluos.test=1 on the
    kernel command line it reports to the console and powers off. The live
    user maluos (casper.conf), the installer and rescue units on tty1, an
    autologin serial getty, the on-media apt source, the MaluOS splash in
    the spinner theme, the medium check and apt timers masked.

